{"id": "EUVD-2026-48782", "enisaUuid": "c10119d7-91bd-330d-8bf5-a4cd041e13cf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: qat - fix VF2PF work teardown race in adf_disable_sriov()\n\nThe VF2PF interrupt handler queues PF-side response work that stores a\nraw pointer to per-VF state (struct adf_accel_vf_info). Currently,\nadf_disable_sriov() destroys per-VF mutexes and frees vf_info without\nstopping new VF2PF work or waiting for in-flight workers to complete. A\nconcurrently scheduled or already queued worker can then dereference\nfreed memory.\n\nThis manifests as a use-after-free when KASAN is enabled:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: null-ptr-deref in mutex_lock+0x76/0xe0\n  Write of size 8 at addr 0000000000000260 by task kworker/24:2/...\n  Workqueue: qat_pf2vf_resp_wq adf_iov_send_resp [intel_qat]\n  Call Trace:\n    kasan_report+0x119/0x140\n    mutex_lock+0x76/0xe0\n    adf_gen4_pfvf_send+0xd4/0x1f0 [intel_qat]\n    adf_recv_and_handle_vf2pf_msg+0x290/0x360 [intel_qat]\n    adf_iov_send_resp+0x8c/0xe0 [intel_qat]\n    process_one_work+0x6ac/0xfd0\n    worker_thread+0x4dd/0xd30\n    kthread+0x326/0x410\n    ret_from_fork+0x33b/0x670\n\nAdd a PF-local flag, vf2pf_disabled, that gates work queueing, worker\nprocessing, and interrupt re-enabling during teardown. Set this flag\natomically with the hardware interrupt mask inside\nadf_disable_all_vf2pf_interrupts(). After masking, synchronize the AE\ncluster MSI-X interrupt and flush the PF response workqueue before\ntearing down per-VF locks and state so all in-flight work completes\nbefore vf_info is destroyed.\n\nIntroduce adf_enable_all_vf2pf_interrupts() to clear the flag and\nunmask all VF2PF interrupts under the same lock when SR-IOV is\nre-enabled. This ensures the software flag and hardware state transition\natomically on both the enable and disable paths.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:51:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:29", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/218c2836b3987f3fa1d9eac505462cded0821e4c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/446b4d77599cf1a168573f7fb32a4a6aa4f09219", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d916c1eae1933511a69bffe243b4ee5d7da399c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f344a369d0380d54c8d6c8d24734a78dd5a89817", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51144032248cc4ea22917370565650670b8b4e9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49cd5ac6de8de39a14ead609bb552d372d5602cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e92b28cd74fa433658efeadf21b9d4b01023d7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/277281c10c63791067d24d421f7c43a15faa9096"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64438", "GHSA-j99q-5p83-43j8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0bcdeccc-c458-3b52-8fa9-b8e80e960b1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "1b15cd8e-cc89-3b2e-a90a-fa2a60b9e72b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "1ea370fc-bc13-3351-9573-847945d99add", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ed8ccaef52fa03fb03cff45b380f72c9f869f273 <218c2836b3987f3fa1d9eac505462cded0821e4c"}, {"id": "27ed352c-c093-35ea-a4d3-3cad3924b9d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ed8ccaef52fa03fb03cff45b380f72c9f869f273 <f344a369d0380d54c8d6c8d24734a78dd5a89817"}, {"id": "2902e58f-5747-3134-99aa-2659739d46d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "4ef87801-2512-35f6-93da-dd31feb40663", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ed8ccaef52fa03fb03cff45b380f72c9f869f273 <446b4d77599cf1a168573f7fb32a4a6aa4f09219"}, {"id": "51628918-4f58-376a-a625-5b8b46fac61d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version"